  "summary": "The ACLU recounts KCUR reporting that Lenexa, Kansas police used ALPRs to track Canyen Ashworth after he wrote an op-ed critical of local police cooperation with ICE, tying him to anti-ICE posters and issuing a 'make your own case' BOLO. The piece frames this as a clear example of ALPR misuse to target protected speech.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Police in Lenexa, Kansas used automated license plate reader (ALPR) technology to pursue a man who wrote a critical op-ed about the police department",
      "paragraph_idx": 1
    },
    {
      "quote": "This is MYOC,\" meaning \"make your own case",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "issuing a BOLO on someone for putting up posters is \"both a rejection of the First Amendment, and a really ridiculous misuse of resources.\"",
